        "bhavartha": "Śiva took the form of a yakṣa; He wears matted hair, holds the Pināka bow in His hand and wears the open directions for His clothes. He is the eternal, divine God. The poet bows to Him as the sound ya, the last syllable of the prayer namaḥ śivāya."
      },
